A||N||7||jhasman||Tach not working||||5||
Z||000000||jhasman||05-19-2001||05:33 PM||||My tachometer in my 88' Fiero Formula does not work. Does the cable need to be replaced? I'm also looking for speaker covers for the speakers by the rear window in the Formula, and a Stock Cassette/Radio deck.<P>Thank you, Jay B. Hasman||||reg||5
Z||000001||Bob Englert||05-19-2001||06:15 PM||||The tach is an electric setup, there is no cable per say.<P>Check the tach filter by the coil (looks like a small metal condenser) to be sure it is connected.  Rodney Dickman makes a replacement if needed.<P>If you have access to another instrument cluster, you might want to swap it to see if that fixes the problem.  The tach itself is fairly easy to swap in the cluster.<BR><P>------------------<BR>Bob<BR>2 - 87 GT's<BR>85 SE 4 cyl||||reg||1
Z||000002||mbramble||05-19-2001||08:28 PM||||What are the symptoms of the tach filter being bad??  Once the engine is started my tach needle moves around to the right and then kind of falls down and hits the oil pressure guage!  When you increase the RPMs it does respond but it just bangs into the oil pressure needle as it tries to come on around back towards zero.  When I shut the engine off it returns to zero.  Does that sound like the filter or the tach???||||reg||1
Z||000003||Max The Chainsaw||05-19-2001||08:54 PM||||Sounds just like what mine did. Tach Filter. If the tach was bad it wouldn't move at all.||||reg||1
Z||000004||varnster||05-20-2001||04:14 PM||||my 87gt tach stoped working I thought it was broke then someone said to drive it(it was in the garage and I only started it to keep the batt charged) so I took it out and after about 10 miles or so wham all went to normal!<BR>you did not mention if you drove it so I thought i would mention it!Good luck.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Hardworker||05-22-2001||01:04 AM||||The tach on my 88 coupe worked when it felt like it.  I removed the top shroud over the instrument panel wiggled a few connectors and it now works like a tach is supposed to.||||reg||1
Z||000006||NASAReeves||05-22-2001||10:01 AM||||Ditto...My tach was working intermittently, and was shaky.  One day, it quit working entirely.  I took the shroud off the back, and discovered that the connector was loose.  Wiggled a few wires & plugged it in well...works like a charm.<P><P>------------------<BR>Scott & Traci<BR>'88 GT||||reg||1
Z||000007||jhasman||05-24-2001||01:04 PM||||THANKS GUYS! I will try your suggestions, and will post the results. Thanks for responding!||||reg||14
